 support=[item('Preventing sickness across all treatment days','Take the written anti-sickness plan even if you feel well. The plan must cover the risk of the medicines on each of Days 1–3 and the two days after the last treatment. Ask the pharmacist to show which medicines are scheduled and which are rescue medicines.',['nccp','antiemetic']),item('One clear steroid plan','The anti-sickness plan may include dexamethasone. Follow the prescribed day-by-day instructions; do not add an extra steroid course or extend it yourself. Tell the team about diabetes, poor sleep or mood changes.',['antiemetic']),item('Fluids and kidney protection','Cisplatin needs IV fluid before and after treatment and may need magnesium/potassium replacement. Your team adapts this for your kidneys, heart and fluid balance. Ask for a personal drinking plan and call if you cannot drink or pass much urine.' if cis else 'Ask for a personal drinking plan. Kidney results help calculate the carboplatin dose; illness or dehydration may require repeat tests. Call if you cannot drink or pass much urine.'),item('If etoposide capsules are prescribed','The source alternative uses capsules on an empty stomach twice daily on Days 2 and 3. Your pharmacy label gives your individual capsule dose. Do not substitute capsules for an infusion yourself, crush/open capsules, double a missed dose or repeat a vomited dose without advice. Obtain safe handling and storage instructions.',['nccp','oral']),item('Medicines, mouth care and infection advice','Check prescriptions, painkillers, supplements and vaccines with the oncology team. Some medicines affect kidney/hearing toxicity or etoposide exposure. Follow mouth-care advice and keep the unit’s urgent contact instructions available.',['nccp','hse'])]
